  "id": "DrugBank_DB11608 - MONDO_grouped_15787_15788",
  "verbalization": "Eftrenonacog Alfa is indicated for Hemophilia, a group of bleeding disorders caused by deficiencies in clotting factors. The evidence suggests that Eftrenonacog Alfa may be used in the treatment of Symptomatic Form Of Hemophilia In Female Carriers, as it shares a common indication with other clotting factor therapies. This relationship is supported by the fact that multiple pathways link Eftrenonacog Alfa to Hemophilia, which in turn is associated with the Symptomatic Form in female carriers. The integration of these pathways implies that Eftrenonacog Alfa may function similarly to other clotting factor replacement therapies in this population. The evidence suggests a potential mechanism of action that aligns with the treatment of hemostatic disorders, particularly in female carriers, where the need for effective clotting factor replacement is critical.",
